WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.487
The teaching database intentionally contains imperfect data.

00:00:03.487 --> 00:00:08.117
Customers includes formatting differences, missing values, and duplicates.

00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:12.697
Products includes inconsistent categories and invalid numeric values.

00:00:12.697 --> 00:00:17.502
Messy customers is a staging table designed for the integrated cleaning project.

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:23.827
The problems are deliberate so that we can practice detection and resolution instead of working with

00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:28.552
already-perfect data. Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:28.552 --> 00:00:33.242
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:39.817
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:44.677
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:49.760
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
